Subject: [PATCH] D5/D6, P0-8 anchored half: the audit chain's head is anchored
 outside the database, and a removal of the newest rows is caught

A sha256 chain shows a row changed or removed from its middle. It cannot show
its newest rows removed (what remains is a valid, shorter chain) or the
database restored from an older backup. The triggers and the grant half of
P0-8 (06152498b) stop the application; they do not stop the owner, a
superuser or a restore. Shown on PostgreSQL 16.13: after a tenant's two newest
rows are removed, verifyAuditChain returns ok.

server/services/audit/chain-anchor.ts: once a day the sweep writes every
tenant's head (row id, chain_seq, sha256_chain, created_at) to the
object-locked evidence bucket, one key per UTC day, written once
(If-None-Match: *). Every run checks every head any anchor names: present
with the same hash is ok; gone but spanned by a batch the archive door
recorded is accounted for; anything else is broken. Every anchor, not only the
latest, because the task can write anchors: a newer one naming an older head
cannot hide a removal an older one records, and the reader treats a second
version or a delete marker on an anchor as broken. A chain that did not verify
is not anchored. Without AUDIT_ANCHOR_BUCKET the check is unverifiable, never
ok.

The sweep gains audit_logs.anchor beside its six stores, on the same alert
path; the alert names a tenant and a row id, never content. The sweep's
ci:tenant-entry-points justification was re-read and holds; its digest only
is refreshed, with a dated note.

Terraform: modules/audit-anchor-access grants the task role PutObject only
with If-None-Match: *, GetObject/GetObjectVersion/ListBucketVersions under the
prefix, and the evidence key only through S3 for this bucket; no delete,
retention, legal-hold or bypass action. Its module test is in CI's matrix.
compliance-evidence exports kms_key_arn; terraform/stack/audit_anchor.tf
instantiates the grant. The one line that hands the task the two variables
is in terraform/stack/main.tf, inside the D1 production-blockers lane's claim,
and is handed to it in docs/work-orders/README.md.

Shown (docs/evidence/D6/2026-10-01-p0-8-anchored-head/):
- dbtest 8/8: truncation, a forged newer anchor, a rewritten head, an anchor
  written twice or hidden, the archive door's record, steady state.
- unit 31/31. Six red against HEAD's sweep.
- Terraform 1.9.8 with the AWS provider mocked: the module 2/2, the stack
  36/36, compliance-evidence 4/4.
- The whole real-database tier: 104 files, 1013 tests.
- tsc 0. All 115 lint-job steps pass. The ESLint ratchet is unchanged.
- Mutations: nine against the application, each red and restored. The ninth,
  m9, is a defect found in review before commit: a configured prefix wrote
  anchors where the check never read them. Six against the grant, each caught
  by its own assertion.

